From: Fedora macchanger maintainers <macchanger-maintainers@fedoraproject.org>
Date: Fri, 4 Jul 2014 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] random: prefer urandom as the seed source

Prefer the nonblocking kernel random source before /dev/random and do not use
the hardware RNG directly. This is the behavior carried by Fedora 44 for
macchanger 1.7.0.

Root cause: upstream 1.7.0 tries /dev/hwrng and blocking /dev/random before
/dev/urandom even though the seed does not require either behavior.
Patch-Source: Fedora 44 macchanger-1.7.0-30.fc44 source RPM,
              macchanger-1.7.0-seed-source.diff
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (existing Fedora downstream patch)
Removal: remove when a stable upstream release uses a suitable nonblocking
         kernel random source first.

---
 src/main.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -97,3 +97,2 @@
-	if ((fd = open("/dev/hwrng", O_RDONLY)) >= 0 ||
-	    (fd = open("/dev/random", O_RDONLY)) >= 0 ||
-	    (fd = open("/dev/urandom", O_RDONLY)) >= 0)
+	if ((fd = open("/dev/urandom", O_RDONLY)) >= 0 ||
+	    (fd = open("/dev/random", O_RDONLY)) >= 0)
--
2.50.1
